      "statement": "For \\(c^\\dagger=(1,-1/4,-3/4)\\), the eight pairs \\((\\theta_t,(\\ell^\\star)^\\top b_t)\\) in lexicographic type order are \\[(0,0),\\ (-3/4,-9/16),\\ (-1/4,-1/16),\\ (-1,-5/8),\\ (1,5/8),\\ (1/4,1/16),\\ (3/4,9/16),\\ (0,0).\\] Hence \\(b_{000}+b_{101}+b_{110}=v\\), \\(0+1/16+9/16=5/8\\), \\(\\kappa(c^\\dagger)=5/8\\), and \\(g^\\star=(1,-1/10,-9/10)\\). The transverse measures satisfy \\(\\sum_t\\lambda_d^+(t)b_t=d^\\dagger\\), \\(\\sum_t\\lambda_d^-(t)b_t=-d^\\dagger\\), total mass two, cost \\(3/16\\), and \\((c^\\dagger)^\\top d^\\dagger=0\\). If \\(n^{-1/3}(3T+2\\varepsilon)\\le1\\), then \\(p_{n,x,h}^\\dagger\\) is a probability law and \\[\\mathbb E[b_t\\mid x,h]=n^{-1/3}(xv+hd^\\dagger),\\quad \\mathbb E[\\theta_t\\mid x,h]=n^{-1/3}x,\\quad \\tau_{c^\\dagger}(m)=n^{-1}\\sum_tm_t\\theta_t.\\] For rational \\(T\\) and \\(\\varepsilon\\), every prior weight \\(\\nu_{n,\\varepsilon,T}^\\dagger(m)\\), likelihood value, and posterior-risk summand is obtained by exact rational integration and integer factorial arithmetic.",
